              "category": "adapter correctness",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalogue_to_extended_crate_codec/encoder.rs",
              "line": 289,
              "message": "Generic parameters decoded into `TypeKindV2::TypeAlias` are dropped during extended-crate encoding: this call passes only `target`, while `encode_type_alias` builds rustdoc generics from `entry.generics()` (the separate type-entry field). For the new wire shape, `entry.generics()` remains empty, so `type Foo<T> = ...` is encoded without `T` and structural comparison reports a mismatch instead of matching the implementation.",
              "severity": "P0"
            }
          ],
