              "category": "adapter correctness",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/tddd/catalogue_document_codec/encode.rs",
              "line": 264,
              "message": "`type_kind_to_dto` validates duplicate names only in the new kind-level list. It serializes those bounds without `validate_bound_str`, and when that list is empty it does not validate the supported legacy `entry_generics` list at all. An in-memory alias with a malformed bound—or legacy generics `[T, T]`—therefore encodes successfully, while `method_generics_from_dtos` rejects the emitted JSON on decode. Validate the effective alias declaration with the same bound and uniqueness rules before emitting it.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
